# chunk-write-padding: pins that writing an `item` or `line` past the end
# first pads the text with its delimiter, or with newline, up to that index
# (chapter 4, Writing chunks). "a,b" has 2 items, so item 4 adds an empty
# item 3: "a,b,,e". A trailing delimiter makes no empty last item, so "a,b,"
# also has 2 items and gives the same "a,b,,e". Empty text has no items, so
# item 2 of it gives ",e". `delimited by ";"` pads with ";". Line 3 of "x"
# pads with two newlines. Fuel, allocation and state figures are estimates.
# Unblessed: the output lines are written by hand, not by bless.

> load padding
> deliver d1 to=padding message=go
> pump clock=2026-09-30T09:00:00Z
seg padding/r1 start delivery=d1 handler=go clause=1 fuel=131 alloc=40 state=76 end=return
run padding/r1 outcome=completed delivery=d1 handler=go fuel=131 alloc=40
pumped state=idle fuel=131

> vars
vars padding row="a,b,,e" trailing="a,b,,e" fromEmpty=",e" semis="a;;c" lined="x" & newline & newline & "z"
